{
  "date": "2026-11-01",
  "compiled": "17:11 AKST",
  "window": "Oct. 29 – Nov. 1, 2026",
  "summary": "Five criminal files were opened at the Fairbanks courthouse on Nov. 1 and four people were arraigned on three of them, among them a domestic violence case charging assault in the fourth degree and three counts of assault when a child is present, and a Delta Junction drunk-driving case filed alongside a fugitive from justice charge against the same man. A court file was also opened behind the Oct. 31 criminal trespass arrest on Old Steese Highway, although no charging document has been filed on it. The Alaska Court System's weekly criminal filings report covers Oct. 25 to Oct. 31 and lists 38 Fairbanks cases, four at Nenana, two at Delta Junction and none at Healy; the court has since filed five more cases at Fairbanks that fall outside that window. Fairbanks Police posted no arrests for Nov. 1 as of 5 p.m., and Alaska State Troopers reported one Interior incident, a missing-persons report involving juveniles in which no offense is alleged.",
  "commentary": null,
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "keith-dv-assault-1101",
      "date": "2026-11-01",
      "place": "Fairbanks",
      "agency": "Alaska Court System",
      "category": "violent",
      "severity": "misdemeanor",
      "cases": [
        "4FA-26-02209CR"
      ],
      "title": "Domestic violence assault charges: Ernest A Keith",
      "body": [
        "Ernest A Keith is charged with assault in the fourth degree — recklessly causing physical injury to another person — and with three counts of assault when a child is present, which is committing an assault while a child is present. All four counts are Class A misdemeanors, and the court file records three of the four as domestic violence related.",
        "The offense is recorded at Fairbanks on Nov. 1 and the charges were filed the same day.",
        "Case 4FA-26-02209CR. He was arraigned Nov. 1 and a public defender was appointed; a pre-trial conference is set for Dec. 24 and a trial week for Jan. 4, 2027. He is charged, not convicted."
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Alaska CourtView",
          "url": "https://records.courts.alaska.gov/eaccess/home.page"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "delong-dui-fugitive-1101",
      "date": "2026-10-31",
      "place": "Delta Junction",
      "agency": "Alaska Court System",
      "category": "dui",
      "severity": "misdemeanor",
      "cases": [
        "4FA-26-02210CR",
        "4FA-26-02211CR"
      ],
      "title": "DUI and fugitive from justice charges: Chad James De Long",
      "body": [
        "Chad James De Long is charged with driving under the influence of alcohol or a controlled substance — operating a vehicle while impaired — with refusal to submit to a chemical test, and with driving while his license was canceled, revoked or suspended for a criminal offense. All three are Class A misdemeanors.",
        "The offense is recorded at Delta Junction on Oct. 31. Case 4FA-26-02210CR, filed at the Fairbanks courthouse on Nov. 1; he was arraigned the same day, with a pre-trial conference set for Dec. 24 and a trial week for Jan. 4, 2027.",
        "A second file, case 4FA-26-02211CR, charges him as a fugitive from justice under the provision for arrest before a requisition — a holding charge used while another state's demand for a person is awaited. Arraignment on that file is set for Nov. 3 and a fugitive from justice hearing for Dec. 1.",
        "He is charged, not convicted."
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Alaska CourtView",
          "url": "https://records.courts.alaska.gov/eaccess/home.page"
        }
      ]
    },
